      "description": "As the first in a series of six language courses, this course invites students without prior knowledge of Russian to explore the basic features of the Russian language. Supported by audiovisual aids, students will receive intensive practice in spoken and written Russian through interactive class work, homework and online exercises. They will become familiar with the basic concepts of Russian grammar and learn how to interact in some simple everyday situations.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "Not for students who have taken RUSS2000,2001,2050,3000 or 3050",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Classwork",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "academic_org": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "learning_outcomes": "Upon successful completion of the course, students should be able to:\n\n• Understand short, simple messages and announcements;\n• read short simple texts and find specific information;\n• communicate in simple, routine situations;\n• write simple notes, messages and short personal letters.\n\nBy the end of the course, students should be able to perform at Level A1.1 of the Common European Framework",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Essays": "10",
        "Essay test or exam": "40",
        "Others": "15",
        "Presentation": "15",
        "Short answer test or exam": "20"
